/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# JS/CSS below are long-lived + immutable (Aug 2026 perf fix), not
# no-cache like the HTML above. Every JS/CSS file across the Hub is
# always referenced with a ?v=N version query string (see the various
# "cache-bust bumps" throughout git history) - a new deploy that
# changes a file's content always changes the URL that references it
# (N goes up), so there's no staleness risk in caching a given
# ?v=N URL forever: it either matches exactly what's currently
# deployed, or it's simply never requested again because the HTML
# that used to reference it now references a newer ?v= instead.
# The HTML files above stay no-cache/must-revalidate specifically
# because THEY aren't versioned themselves - they're what tells the
# browser which ?v=N to ask for next, so they always need a fresh
# check. Confirmed via full-repo audit (Aug 2026) that every local
# <script src> and <link rel="stylesheet"> in every tool references
# its target with ?v=N - if a new one is ever added without one, it
# will get stuck cached under this policy until manually version-
# tagged, so keep that convention going for any new file references.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
